p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 470)</h2>
<p><b>The originals answer whenever you stop to look.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Optimised media now works the way it should:</b> the stand-in carries playback, and the moment you pause, zoom past 1:1 or open the scopes, the real frame is fetched and shown. The OPTIMISED badge disappears while you're on the original, so its presence answers "am I looking at the real thing?" without a label.</li>
<li><b>Delete Optimised Media for This Shot / for the Session</b> — it's meant to be disposable, and now it's one menu item. Tells you how much it freed.</li>
<li><b>You're warned before a session goes out without stand-ins</b> — when sharing to the web or sending an invite — with Optimise Now offered right there. It only warns about shots that would actually be painful for a remote seat, not the ones that play fine anywhere.</li>
<li><b>Progress while optimising</b>, per shot and percentage.</li>
<li><b>Render on another Mac.</b> Settings ▸ a host name, and the same job runs there over ssh. It's the same <code>Asobi optimise</code> command the app runs, which is also available headless so a coordinator can pre-render a review before anyone opens it.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
